# Documentation Maintenance Protocol

Every change to AI Job Agent MUST update relevant documentation. Documentation is not optional.

## Change → Document Mapping

| Change Type | Required Updates |
|-------------|-----------------|
| New feature / user-facing behavior | PRD.md, HLD.md, LLD.md, README.md |
| New API endpoint | LLD.md §3, API_SPEC.md |
| New/modified collection | LLD.md §5, DATABASE.md |
| New Celery worker/queue | HLD.md §8-9, LLD.md §8-9 |
| New scheduler job | HLD.md §9, LLD.md §10, configs/scheduler.yaml |
| New AI prompt | AI_PROMPTS.md, prompts/*.md, configs/ai.yaml |
| New job collector | LLD.md §12, configs/job_sources.yaml |
| New React page/component | LLD.md §15-17 |
| New env variable | .env.example, LLD.md §20, DEPLOYMENT.md |
| Docker/infra change | DEPLOYMENT.md, docker-compose.yml |
| Architecture change | HLD.md, ARCHITECTURE.md |
| Security change | SECURITY.md |
| New coding pattern | CODING_GUIDELINES.md |

## Version Tracking

When updating any doc, increment the version table at the bottom of that document.

## No Stale Docs

If you change code and docs are stale, the change is **incomplete**. Finish doc updates before marking the task done.
